Step 11.3 is complete. All four verification gates are green: 372 backend tests (10 live skipped, 112 subtests), 154 frontend tests, the Vite production build, and the generated-doc drift check.

## What changed

**New: `studio/shared/providers_common/settings_schema.py`** — the leaf of the settings import chain. Owns `SENSITIVE_KEYS_RE`, the `"***"` sentinel, the §22.2 widget vocabulary, `ui.show_if` evaluation, schema validation, `split_settings`, `redact`, `apply_settings_patch`, and `invocation_config`. Nothing now imports settings *storage* to learn what a secret is.

**Manifest v2** — `description`, `docs_url`, `environment`, plus `public_dict()`, the §25 representation that round-trips through `validate_manifest` for every shipped manifest and carries no env names, callables, or paths. Validation rejects non-`https` doc URLs, oversized/control-character descriptions, and malformed env names.

**Availability + health** (deferred D9/D10 from 11.2) — `availability()` implements §21.5 (`available` / `needs_configuration` / `degraded`), computed from `requires` *after* env fallback so present-but-empty `api_key` values are not mistaken for configuration. A provider with no `health_check` now returns `unknown`, not `ok`.

**Environment as read-time fallback** — `resolve_settings()` feeds provider validation/health/invocation only; never written back, never serialized. `_seed_from_env` stopped copying the three API keys and stopped writing `selected_provider` (the `INWORLD_API_KEY` side effect is gone).

**Secrets are write-only** — the §22.6 live defect is fixed rather than deferred: both GET routes are redacted, and all write paths restore a sentinel submission from the stored value, so the whole-blob round-trip in `useProviders.js` cannot erase a key.

**Migrations** — `apply_migrations` was structurally incapable of running an upgrade (it skipped every version `>=` the stored one). Now keyed on target version, running ascending, stamping per step. v2 adopts the legacy `app-config.json` selections through the alias table. The repo's own `settings.json` migrated on this run with all selections preserved.

## Two things worth flagging

- **A leak I found and closed:** `_kie_ai_options` merged the whole `kie_ai` settings dict — including `api_key` — into `grabber_job.json` under `output/`, which project archives copy. `kie_ai_generate()` resolves the key itself and never read it there, so both call sites now merge only the portable half.
- **I did not invent a `deprecated` manifest field.** The step text names it, but §20.1 and §25 are frozen without one. Deprecation is carried by `aliases` instead — the §14.4 legacy wire strings are now declared on the five providers that own them. Likewise the shipped manifests stay at `contract_version=1`, since `2` claims invocability that 11.4 hasn't built yet. Both adjustments are recorded in the plan.

Nothing is committed yet — say the word and I'll create the `step 11.3` commit.

